# Reference
- Code sample: `C:\Game\Arena\Narxim-GAS-Example\Source\GAS_Example`
- Before writing GAS, a gameplay ability, an attribute set, or Enhanced Input for an ability, read the matching file there and follow that procedure.
- Tranek in `gas.mdc` is the concept reference. Narxim is the code reference.
- Narxim is Unreal 5.6. This project is 5.8.1. Copy the procedure, not the engine version.

# Overrides gas.mdc
- The ASC stays on the figure, the entity that owns the stats. Do not move it to PlayerState. One player fields several figures.
- Init on the server in `PossessedBy`, and on the client when the owning state replicates. Same order as `Characters/CharacterBase.cpp`.

# Abilities and input
- A new ability is its own `JoA_GAS_` class, in the style of `AbilitySystem/GameplayAbilities/CustomGameplayAbility`.
- The ability holds the `UInputAction`. Bind it on the Enhanced Input component in `OnGiveAbility`. Clear that binding when the ability is removed.
- Wait for input inside an ability with an ability task, as in `AbilitySystem/AbilityTasks/AbilityTask_WaitEnhancedInputEvent`.
- Do not bind gameplay actions as one-off test keys on the player controller.

# Attributes and effects
- Split attribute sets by concern. Replicate them with `DOREPLIFETIME_WITH_PARAMS_FAST` and `bIsPushBased`, as in `AttributeSets/HealthAttributeSet.cpp`.
- Damage and healing go through a meta attribute and a server execution, not a direct SetByCaller write onto Health.
- The server grants starting sets, abilities, effects, and tags from one initialization struct. See `AbilitySystem/Data/AbilitySystemData.h` and `InitializeAbilitySystemData`.
- A turn-based damage-over-time or buff follows `AbilitySystem/GameplayEffects/TurnBased`, not a real-time periodic effect.

# Do not copy
- Iris stays the replication path for the board, cells, and figure state. GAS attribute data stays on the push model above.
- Do not set a 100 Hz net update frequency.
- Do not bring movement, CommonUI, Model View ViewModel, or the AGRPRO plugin.
